# Object Explorer & Filtering System

## Architecture Overview

```
ObjectExplorer              ← renders VirtualTreeItem tree from Speckle world tree
  ├─ useSpeckleTree         ← flattens tree, manages expansion/selection
  ├─ useSpeckleFiltering    ← hide/show/isolate via FilteringExtension
  └─ useSpeckleInteractions ← hover highlight, zoom-to

useAcousticLayerIsolation   ← manages acoustic-layer-specific isolate/hide state
                               across Acoustic ↔ Default viewMode switches
                               (runs in SpeckleScene, NOT in ObjectExplorer)
```

## View Modes

| Mode      | Behavior |
|-----------|----------|
| `default` | All objects visible. Acoustic layer objects are **hidden** in the 3D viewer (via `useAcousticLayerIsolation`) but visible in the ObjectExplorer tree. ObjectExplorer hide/isolate controls are active. |
| `acoustic`| **Only** the acoustic layer is isolated (ghosted others). ObjectExplorer tree filters to acoustic layer subtree only. Hide/isolate buttons are hidden; toggle-visibility switches to isolate/un-isolate. |
| `dark`    | All filtering disabled; `applyFilterColors()` returns early. UI-only mode. |

View mode is **not persisted** through Zustand `persist` — it's stored in a separate `localStorage` key `compas-view-mode` and restored 300ms after viewer init in `SpeckleScene.tsx`.

## ObjectExplorer — Hide & Isolate

Two distinct buttons per tree item:

| Button  | Method | Speckle call | Collision risk |
|---------|--------|-------------|----------------|
| Hide/Show | `hideObjects` / `showObjects` | `hideObjects(ids, stateKey)` | None — `ghost=false` |
| Isolate | `isolateObjects` | `isolateObjects(ids, stateKey, true, true)` | High — `ghost=true` |

In `acoustic` mode: the isolate button is hidden (`hideIsolateButton=true`), and the visibility toggle delegates to isolate/un-isolate instead of hide/show.

The ObjectExplorer's `stateKey` is `'explorer-default'`. The acoustic layer's `stateKey` is `'acoustic-materials'`. These are DIFFERENT keys, but Speckle does NOT compose state across keys — see "FilteringExtension Mutex" below.

## FilteringExtension — Mutually Exclusive Operations

**`ext.isolateObjects` and `ext.hideObjects` are mutually exclusive regardless of `stateKey`.** The last call wins — calling one clears the state set by the other.

### Compose Pattern

When you need both isolate and hide simultaneously, compose them in a single synchronous block:

```typescript
// isolate → re-hide → re-isolate → render
ext.isolateObjects(targetIds, 'explorer-default', true, true);
reapplyPostIsolateHides();                         // ext.hideObjects on acoustic-materials key
ext.isolateObjects(targetIds, 'explorer-default', true, true); // re-establish after hide cleared it
viewerRef.current?.requestRender();
```

### unIsolateObjects Pitfall

`ext.unIsolateObjects` clears **ALL** isolation for the given `stateKey`, not just the specified IDs. To remove specific IDs while keeping others:

```typescript
const remaining = existingIds.filter((id) => !idsToRemove.includes(id));
if (remaining.length > 0) {
  ext.isolateObjects(remaining, stateKey, true, true); // re-isolate remaining
} else {
  ext.unIsolateObjects(objectIds, stateKey, true, false);
}
```

### Re-apply Guard

Any rAF/setInterval loop that calls `ext.hideObjects` will clear active isolation. **Always check for active isolation before re-hiding:**

```typescript
const explorerIsolated = getExplorerIsolatedIds('explorer-default');
if (explorerIsolated && explorerIsolated.length > 0) return; // skip re-hide
```

## useAcousticLayerIsolation — Five Sections

| § | Purpose | When |
|---|---------|------|
| 1  | Show acoustic objects | Entering Acoustic mode |
| 1b | Hide acoustic objects | First load in Default mode |
| 2  | Auto-detect "Acoustics" layer | World tree loads |
| 3  | Apply/remove acoustic isolation | viewMode or layerId changes |
| 4  | Open ObjectExplorer in selection mode | Entering Acoustic mode, no layer set |
| 5  | Re-apply isolate/hide state (rAF loop) | Every frame |

`hiddenGeometryIdsRef` tracks which acoustic-layer geometry IDs should be hidden in default mode. Synced to `speckleStore.setPostIsolateHideIds()` so `useSpeckleFiltering` can re-hide after each isolate/un-isolate call.

## Key Files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `ObjectExplorer.tsx` | Tree UI, dispatches hide/isolate to `useSpeckleFiltering` |
| `useSpeckleFiltering.ts` | Hide/show/isolate/un-isolate via FilteringExtension, compose pattern, tracked in `speckleStore` |
| `useAcousticLayerIsolation.ts` | Acoustic-layer-specific visibility management across viewMode switches |
| `speckleStore.ts` | Module-level refs for `_postIsolateHideIds`, tracking functions, `applyFilterColors` |
| `acousticLayerStore.ts` | Persisted acoustic layer selection (which layer = "Acoustics") |
| `VirtualTreeItem.tsx` | Renders a single tree row with hide/isolate buttons |
